<Solution> <!-- Define the solution that groups the application project and supported build platforms below. Angle syntax: The < and > bound the opening Solution tag; attributes describe this element, and its child elements continue until the matching closing tag below. The angle symbols at the comment boundaries enclose this explanation as XML commentary, which the application and build tools ignore. -->
  <Configurations> <!-- Group the solution platforms available for the project reference below. Angle syntax: The < and > bound the opening Configurations tag; attributes describe this element, and its child elements continue until the matching closing tag below. The angle symbols at the comment boundaries enclose this explanation as XML commentary, which the application and build tools ignore. -->
    <Platform Name="x64" /> <!-- Expose the x64 platform as a selectable solution build target. Angle syntax: The < and > bound a self-closing Platform element; the slash means this single line supplies the element without a separate closing tag. The angle symbols at the comment boundaries enclose this explanation as XML commentary, which the application and build tools ignore. -->
    <Platform Name="x86" /> <!-- Expose the x86 platform as a selectable solution build target. Angle syntax: The < and > bound a self-closing Platform element; the slash means this single line supplies the element without a separate closing tag. The angle symbols at the comment boundaries enclose this explanation as XML commentary, which the application and build tools ignore. -->
  </Configurations> <!-- Close Configurations; following elements return to its parent. Angle syntax: The < and > bound a closing Configurations tag, and the slash identifies the end of the matching group opened above. The angle symbols at the comment boundaries enclose this explanation as XML commentary, which the application and build tools ignore. -->
  <Project Path="Bitreader.vcxproj" /> <!-- Include Bitreader.vcxproj in this solution so its listed source and model files can be built together. Angle syntax: The < and > bound a self-closing Project element; the slash means this single line supplies the element without a separate closing tag. The angle symbols at the comment boundaries enclose this explanation as XML commentary, which the application and build tools ignore. -->
</Solution> <!-- Close Solution; following elements return to its parent. Angle syntax: The < and > bound a closing Solution tag, and the slash identifies the end of the matching group opened above. The angle symbols at the comment boundaries enclose this explanation as XML commentary, which the application and build tools ignore. -->
